arm: allow cp10/cp11 access around disableFpu() during boot

With CONFIG_HAVE_FPU disabled (as in ARM_bcm2837_verified), seL4 17.0.0
fpsimd_HWCapTest() restores CPACR to CPACR_DEFAULT, which denies cp10 and
cp11. init_cpu() then calls disableFpu(), which reads FPEXC with vmrs and
takes an Undefined Instruction exception. Grant cp10/cp11 access only for
the disableFpu() call and restore CPACR_DEFAULT afterwards.

Applied by tools/prepare-sel4-source.sh to a copy of vendor/seL4.
Remove this patch once upstream seL4 fixes the issue.
See research/sel4/verified-config-deviations.md.

--- a/src/arch/arm/kernel/boot.c
+++ b/src/arch/arm/kernel/boot.c
@@ -239,7 +239,11 @@
 
     /* Disable FPU to avoid channels where a platform has an FPU but doesn't make use of it */
     if (haveHWFPU) {
+        setCPACR(CPACR_FPU_ENABLE);
+        isb();
         disableFpu();
+        setCPACR(CPACR_DEFAULT);
+        isb();
     }
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_HAVE_FPU
